  "worked_solution": "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=1i+2j,\\,u=3i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the drone after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(3i-2j)(3) \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(9i-6j) \\\\  & =(10i-4j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the drone to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i-4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{116} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{29}\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
